  "facts": [
    "The Liberty Bridge, opened in 1896, was the first Budapest bridge to be rebuilt after World War II, showcasing resilience and engineering prowess amid the city’s wartime devastation.",
    "Designed by János Feketeházy, the 333.6‑meter cantilever truss bridge imitates a chain‑type aesthetic, blending Art Nouveau flair with functional strength for trams and vehicles.",
    "Atop its four masts, bronze Turul statues—mythical falcon‑like birds—celebrate Hungarian heritage, making the Liberty Bridge a living canvas of national symbolism."
